cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SkewAdam in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: SkewAdam
abstract: >-
  Tiered optimizer state allocation for memory-efficient Mixture-of-Experts
  training. Momentum is kept only on the dense backbone, the experts keep a
  factored second moment alone, and the router keeps an exact second moment,
  cutting optimizer state to 2.6% of AdamW's on a 6.78B-parameter MoE.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuemaan/skewadam"
authors:
